response.content:
{
  "claims": [
    "The withdrawal rate of medications for the Heart Failure (hf_lombardia_v1) pathway in the cooperative coop_3 is 89.01%, significantly below the regional alarm threshold (5 percentage points below 100%), while the rest of the ATS stands at 99.92%.",
    "In the commune of Camisano, the medication withdrawal rate is 81.82%; in Fiesco it is 76.92%; in Izano it is 74.07%; in Madignano it is 87.5%; in Montodine it is 82.76%; in Pianengo it is 90.00%; in Ricengo it is 86.67%; in Ripalta Arpina it is 85.71%; in Romanengo it is 89.47%; and in Soncino it is 87.62%. The rest of the ATS has a rate of 99.45%.",
    "The medication withdrawal rate by age shows no significant differences: for patients aged 65-74 years it is 99.13%; for those aged 75-84 years it is 98.85%; for those aged 85 and over it is 99.10%; and for those under 65 years it is 99.03%. No value is available for the rest of the ATS in this age segmentation."
  ],
  "conclusion": "The issue is primarily localized in the communes of Camisano, Fiesco, Izano, and Montodine, where medication withdrawal rates are below 83%. The cooperative coop_3, which includes these communes, has an overall rate of 89.01%, consistent with local data. The intervention margin is concentrated in the communes with the lowest rates, particularly Fiesco (76.92%) and Izano (74.07%). The recommended action is a targeted intervention in these communes, focusing on patient support, prescription verification, and potential reactivation of communication channels with GPs."
}
